    "created_at": "2021-06-29T23:05:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-06-29T23:05:31Z",
    "body": "It's unclear what the benefit of the proposed change is. It doesn't save significant typing (just `new`); in cases where you want to avoid allocating a new instance, the encoder/decoder can be cached and used statelessly.\r\n\r\nGiven a time machine to redesign the API now that streams are a thing, this makes more sense for non-streaming encodes/decodes, but is it worth adding to the platform?",
