    "updated_at": "2022-03-04T00:40:28Z",
    "body": "> since the WebIDL layer is a perf bottle neck\r\n\r\n@hsivonen How so? In Deno we have an optimized path in our WebIDL bindings for this specific API that bypasses the slow USVString conversion completely. This should be possible in other implementations too.\r\n\r\nDuring encode you can convert the first argument to a DOMString (which is fast), and then just perform a lenient UTF-8 encoding on that string, which will already perform lone surrogate conversion. https://github.com/denoland/deno/blob/main/ext/web/08_text_encoding.js#L166-L175",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
